# The bashOS layer on Arch (Amrchy) — the same groups as ../base.list, in Arch's package names.
# Amrchy's own install set already carries most of them (tmux, git, jq, ripgrep, fd, bat, btop,
# avahi, nss-mdns, ufw, openssh); `bashos os install` adds only what is missing, with pacman.
# Line format as ../base.list: package names, then an optional `cmd:NAME` guard.

# runtime: the kernel's Python (venv is part of it on Arch), the refine loop's shellcheck, the
# engine's Node (Amrchy installs Node through mise: its shim satisfies the guard)
python
shellcheck
nodejs npm cmd:node
git ca-certificates curl rsync

# the console: one shared tmux session on the desktop and every ssh login
tmux zsh sudo less

# what the probes and the verdict floor read
procps-ng iproute2 lm_sensors smartmontools
jq ripgrep fd bat btop

# reaching the box: ssh, mDNS (HOST.local), a firewall
openssh avahi nss-mdns ufw
